{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Then Jacob answered, etc.</b> That is: I do not deny that I fled, and as for your saying ״why״ etc. — it was because I feared you, lest you might seize etc. And as for what you were thinking to say, that for this reason I stole your elohim so that they would not inform — to this he answered ״with whomever״ etc. For this claim, that the theft of the teraphim was because he was fleeing (for this would inform that he was a fugitive), is a plausible claim; therefore he swore to him upon it with an oath of imprecation, according to the law of one who pronounces an oath of imprecation in a case of doubt."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:17.367679490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}